  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1970s, a man named Ted Owens, who claimed psychic powers, contacted the physicists Hal Puthoff and Russell Targ at the Stanford Research Institute, a California research lab where they were testing psychics, and was turned away. Jeffrey Mishlove, a researcher with a PhD who studies psychic phenomena, tells Michels that Owens asked them why they were wasting time with the performer Uri Geller when he, Owens, was \"the world's greatest subject\"."
